"Kent Paul Dolan" <xanthian@well.com> writes:
> Said another way, do trapdoor fall-throughs sit in
> some pending queue and get distributed on the level
> where they land after it is either newly generated
> _or_ selected as a bones level,

Yes. The migrating monster list gets checked after the level is
generated/loaded/reloaded, and anything that's scheduled to be placed
there is so; mon_arrive() doesn't know or care whether the level has
been created from scratch, loaded as bones, or previously visited that
game.

> so that a bones level might not be identical, by the time I first
> see it, to its state at the death of the former PC???

For literal values of "see it", yes, since vision on a new level is
first calculated after migrating objects and monsters arrive.

> That could get supremely ugly, if Big Nasties from
> my game fall through to join forces with whatever
> killed the bones file's previous PC.

Yes.

